From 23327dca1bedd964e1be27d8e828c735b14e7ac3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:42:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Routing: let pets shimmy, prefer shorter shimmies, tighten
 straight gaps

Pets: TemplateDog/TemplateCat (ExpansionPack5.far, STR 150 entries 11-18)
have no side-step animation, so pets squeeze through a pinch facing
forwards with their normal walk cycle, at velocity 4 (their move frames
are already doubled, so this matches the Sims' 1/4 walking speed).

Cost: a shimmy leg now costs its length + 4 instead of 4x length + 16.
The time-based cost made Sims walk around every pinch wider than
chair-to-chair (e.g. a 1-tile table and a chair touching diagonally),
which players read as not finding the obvious route.

Straight gaps between parallel edges must be at least 5 units wide
(diagonal corners keep the 3-unit minimum), so a gap of half a Sim is
never squeezed through. Two chairs side by side (gap 6) still count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019q6m8f542cVUMKg755aFtZ
